# Spec §6.2 (Cambios sin guardar: what counts as "there are changes"). It is tested
# by closing with the X: without changes it closes directly ("nada" stays open); with
# changes it opens the close notice ("el panel con el aviso de cierre").
# "There are changes" is when Guardar would change something relative to the values the
# panel was opened with: typing and returning to the original value does not count, nor do
# the spaces Guardar trims, nor the order of the schedule windows; an
# emptied field or an empty schedule row does count. It is measured against what the panel had on opening,
# not against what another device wrote. When editing, the task opens as
# one-off and without a schedule unless the step says
# otherwise. The notice itself is verified in aviso-de-cierre.feature.
Feature: Unsaved changes

  # Unsaved changes 1
  # When editing, a field with another value is a change; with the same value, it is not.
  Scenario Outline: Unsaved changes 1
    Given I open the panel to edit the task <title> with note <note>
    When I type <value> in the field <field>
    And I tap the X of the panel
    Then what stays open is <open>

    Examples:
      | title  | note | field                   | value     | open                            |
      | Pagar  | Luz  | Título                  | Pagar luz | el panel con el aviso de cierre |
      | Pagar  | Luz  | Nota                    | Gas       | el panel con el aviso de cierre |
      | Pagar  | Luz  | Título                  | Pagar     | nada                            |
      | Pagar  | Luz  | Nota                    | Luz       | nada                            |

  # Unsaved changes 2
  # Typing and returning to the original value does not count as a change; returning to another
  # value does.
  Scenario Outline: Unsaved changes 2
    Given I open the panel to edit the task <title> with note <note>
    When I type <first> in the field <field>
    And I type <second> in the field <field>
    And I tap the X of the panel
    Then what stays open is <open>

    Examples:
      | title  | note | field  | first     | second    | open                            |
      | Pagar  | Luz  | Título | Pagar luz | Pagar     | nada                            |
      | Pagar  | Luz  | Título | Pagar luz | Pagar gas | el panel con el aviso de cierre |
      | Pagar  | Luz  | Nota   | Gas       | Luz       | nada                            |
      | Pagar  | Luz  | Nota   | Gas       | Agua      | el panel con el aviso de cierre |

  # Unsaved changes 3
  # The spaces Guardar trims (title and note) do not count.
  Scenario Outline: Unsaved changes 3
    Given I open the panel to edit the task <title> with note <note>
    When I type <value> with spaces around it in the field <field>
    And I tap the X of the panel
    Then what stays open is <open>

    Examples:
      | title  | note | field                   | value     | open                            |
      | Pagar  | Luz  | Título                  | Pagar     | nada                            |
      | Pagar  | Luz  | Título                  | Pagar luz | el panel con el aviso de cierre |
      | Pagar  | Luz  | Nota                    | Luz       | nada                            |
      | Pagar  | Luz  | Nota                    | Gas       | el panel con el aviso de cierre |

